  "title": "Numbers",
  "description": "Stereoelectroencephalography (sEEG) recordings from epilepsy patients at Oregon Health & Science University, collected while they were in the epilepsy monitoring unit awaiting seizures. Participants were presented with auditory and visual numerical stimuli, either symbolic (Arabic numerals and spoken numbers) or non-symbolic (dots and beeps). The dataset supports investigation of the neural representation of numerical quantity across modalities and formats.",
  "methods_description": "Intracranial stereoelectroencephalography was recorded from epilepsy patients in the epilepsy monitoring unit while they viewed and heard symbolic (Arabic digits, spoken numbers) and non-symbolic (dot arrays, beeps) numerical stimuli.",
